{# THE SECTION'S FIRST SCREEN — how big this installation is, and what it
   gives you.

   THE FIGURE ROW IS SETTLED AND IS HERE. Four to a row, and not one of them
   the section's own: how many modules run is the catalogue's answer, how many
   areas is the areas', how many people is the team's, and what is kept is
   whoever keeps it. A row that any one package had written would be four
   numbers nobody owns.

   THE REST OF THE BODY IS BEING AMENDED and is deliberately not drawn yet.
   The owner ruled that what a fresh installation is told at `/` today keeps a
   PERMANENT home on this screen — what the installation gives you, evergreen,
   with a next-steps list that is true at any age rather than only on the
   first day — and the amendment drawing it is in hand. Drawing the previous
   composition here and replacing it in a week would put a screen in front of
   people twice. #}
{% extends '@Shell/settings/_section.html.twig' %}

{% block shell_page %}
    {{ include('@Shell/settings/_figures.html.twig', {figures: settings.figures}, with_context: false) }}

    {{ include('@Shell/_page_hint.html.twig', {
        lead: 'The rest of this screen is being drawn.',
        say: 'What this installation gives you, and what to do next at any age of it, land here. What is installed and at what version is on the Installation tab; the catalogue is on Modules; who this belongs to is on Organisation.',
    }, with_context: false) }}
{% endblock %}
